From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:41:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: retrieve MAC address from system firmware if
 provided

Some devices have no useful MAC address in the WLAN module itself. On
the Surface Laptop 8, for example, the WCN7850 advertises a random
address, while the address assigned to the machine is known to the
system firmware. The boot loader can pass it to Linux, for example as a
"local-mac-address" property in the device tree node of the PCIe device,
but ath12k never looks for it.

Use the generic device helper to retrieve the address, as ath11k does
since commit 176239a9a2e3 ("wifi: ath11k: retrieve MAC address from
system firmware if provided"), and keep ath11k's order: per-radio
addresses reported by the target come first, then the system firmware
address, then the address the target advertises. The system firmware
address takes the place of the target's base address, so the radio index
is added to it as before, and a wiphy with several radios uses it as its
permanent address.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
index 2c51d3567fd..b609198b19e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -14815,15 +14815,30 @@ static int ath12k_mac_hw_register(struct ath12k_hw *ah)
 	bool is_6ghz = false, is_raw_mode = false, is_monitor_disable = false;
 	u8 *mac_addr = NULL;
 	u8 mbssid_max_interfaces = 0;
+	u8 fw_mac_addr[ETH_ALEN] = {};
 
 	wiphy->max_ap_assoc_sta = 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * Devices without a useful address in the WLAN module get one from the
+	 * system firmware (e.g. device tree "local-mac-address", set by the
+	 * boot loader). As in ath11k, per-radio addresses from the target take
+	 * precedence; otherwise prefer the system firmware address over the
+	 * one the target advertises.
+	 */
+	if (ab->pdevs_macaddr_valid ||
+	    device_get_mac_address(ab->dev, fw_mac_addr))
+		eth_zero_addr(fw_mac_addr);
+
 	for_each_ar(ah, ar, i) {
 		u32 ht_cap_info = 0;
 
 		pdev = ar->pdev;
 		if (ar->ab->pdevs_macaddr_valid) {
 			ether_addr_copy(ar->mac_addr, pdev->mac_addr);
+		} else if (!is_zero_ether_addr(fw_mac_addr)) {
+			ether_addr_copy(ar->mac_addr, fw_mac_addr);
+			ar->mac_addr[4] += ar->pdev_idx;
 		} else {
 			ether_addr_copy(ar->mac_addr, ar->ab->mac_addr);
 			ar->mac_addr[4] += ar->pdev_idx;
@@ -14859,6 +14874,8 @@ static int ath12k_mac_hw_register(struct ath12k_hw *ah)
 
 		if (i == 0)
 			mac_addr = ar->mac_addr;
+		else if (!is_zero_ether_addr(fw_mac_addr))
+			mac_addr = fw_mac_addr;
 		else
 			mac_addr = ab->mac_addr;
 
-- 
